Usages:
  category_taxonomy: |
    LoggerCategory is a fixed, alphabetically-sorted enum of subsystem tags (e.g. tabs,
    coordinator, redux, storage, sync, telemetry, webview). Every call site picks the category
    matching the subsystem doing the logging; new categories are added to this single enum only
    after team discussion, never invented ad hoc per call site.
  level_semantics: |
    LoggerLevel is one of debug (diagnostics/tests only), info (normal expected behavior),
    warning (unexpected but recoverable), fatal (the application cannot continue correctly, e.g.
    a data store it depends on failed). Pick the lowest level that still gets the message the
    attention it needs.

Annotations: |
  This cell is the app's single logging facade: one protocol (`Logger`) implemented by one
  concrete type (`DefaultLogger`) that fans a log call out to local file storage, the console,
  and Sentry crash/error reporting. Every other cell that needs to log takes a `Logger` (usually
  defaulted to the shared `DefaultLogger` instance) rather than talking to SwiftyBeaver/Sentry
  directly.

  Use `category_taxonomy` and `level_semantics` when constructing a log call.

---

"Logger()":
  location: Logger.swift
  annotations: |
    Contract for the app's logging facade. The crashedLastLaunch property lets callers show
    "we recovered from a crash" UI without depending on the crash-reporting backend directly.
  properties:
    "crashedLastLaunch -> Bool": |
      Whether the previous app launch ended in a crash, as determined by the crash-reporting
      backend.
  methods:
    "setup(sendCrashReports: Bool)": |
      Initialize the underlying crash-reporting backend for this process.

      `sendCrashReports`: whether the user has opted in to sending crash/error reports
    "logCustomError(error: Error)": |
      Record an Error value as its own event, separate from a plain text log call.
    "log(message: String, level: LoggerLevel, category: LoggerCategory, extra: [String: String]?, description: String?, file: String, function: String, line: Int)": |
      Record one log message locally, to the console, and to the crash-reporting backend.

      Use `category_taxonomy` to pick `category` and `level_semantics` to pick `level`.

      `message`: the primary log text
      `extra`: optional structured key/value context attached to the event
      `description`: optional human-readable elaboration appended to `message`
      `file`, `function`, `line`: call-site location, defaulted by the caller's compiler
      directives
    "copyLogsToDocuments()": |
      Copy the on-disk log files into the app's Documents folder, so they can be pulled off a
      device (e.g. via file sharing) for debugging.
    "deleteCachedLogFiles()": |
      Delete the on-disk log files.

"Logger::DefaultLogger()":
  location: DefaultLogger.swift
  annotations: |
    The one concrete `Logger` used by the running app, exposed as a shared singleton instance:
    SwiftyBeaver for local/console output, plus a crash-reporting backend for fatal-and-above
    events and custom errors.
  properties:
    "shared -> DefaultLogger": |
      The single, process-wide logger instance every other cell defaults to.
    "crashedLastLaunch -> Bool": |
      Concrete crashedLastLaunch, backed by the crash-reporting backend.

